{
 "format": {
  "name": "tessel",
  "version": 1
 },
 "meta": {
  "title": "Newsletter email",
  "description": "An email, 600 wide (never a post): the Email frame is the email's card and each child is a section, top to bottom. Restyle it in the brand with set_tokens (color.brand for the button and pill, color.ink, color.paper the card, color.page around it, color.night the footer; font.heading, font.body), put the business's name in Logo and FooterName (or replace Logo with the logo as an image layer named for its alt text) and its own words everywhere. {{field}} words are filled for each person; keep them. A layer named link:<address> links: rename it to the real address. Save it as a template with email_design_save, declaring its fields. A newsletter (marketing with a topic, sent with email_campaign): a headline and lede, a Photo (a grey box: replace it with an image layer of the person's photo, named for its alt text, or delete it), a feature with a button, two stories side by side that stack on a phone (Stories: semantic columns), a closing line. No fields beyond the person's. Marketing: keep Unsubscribe and {{address}} in the footer."
 },
